From: FlexVM maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: x86: initialize the TSC multiplier before setting its rate

A newly allocated vCPU has zero TSC scaling ratios. The initial frequency
request can fail, or select software catchup, without setting a multiplier
when hardware TSC scaling is unavailable. vCPU creation intentionally does
not reject that frequency, so initialize a safe unity multiplier first.
This preserves subsequent KVM_SET_TSC_KHZ validation and valid scaling.

--- a/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
@@ -12035,6 +12035,12 @@
 	kvm_xen_init_vcpu(vcpu);
 	kvm_vcpu_mtrr_init(vcpu);
 	vcpu_load(vcpu);
+	/*
+	 * Initial frequency setup can fail or select catchup without writing a
+	 * multiplier. Keep the TSC running even without hardware scaling.
+	 */
+	kvm_vcpu_write_tsc_multiplier(vcpu,
+				    kvm_caps.default_tsc_scaling_ratio);
 	kvm_set_tsc_khz(vcpu, vcpu->kvm->arch.default_tsc_khz);
 	kvm_vcpu_reset(vcpu, false);
 	kvm_init_mmu(vcpu);
